Darklon wrote:
>
> Is there any penalty for magic users the heavier armours?
> (ring,chain,plate), does it effect your spellcasting?

It isn't quite about weight.  The heaviest armor is crystal plate mail
and it does not interfere with spell casting.  It's mostly about metal. 

Learn the material that a piece of armor is made from then check your
failure rate.  Then put it on and check your failure rate.  The
comparison will show you that metal armor interferes the most.

The fun part is the "exception that proves the rule".  There are a small
number of types that improve casting.


